# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Mag-map ng mga representasyon ng operator para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Qiskit bosons"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations"
msgstr "Mag-map ng mga representasyon ng operator"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mappers-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations {#map-operator-representations}"
msgstr "Mag-map ng mga representasyon ng operator {#map-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **mapper** turns a [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") into a qubit operator, here a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). The operator itself knows nothing about qubits: it stores ladder operators on modes, and a bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many particles. Everything that makes the operator finite (how many occupation levels you keep, and how those levels are laid out on qubits) is decided when you map it.\n"
msgstr "Ginagawang qubit operator ng isang **mapper** ang isang [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\"), dito ay isang [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). Walang alam ang operator mismo tungkol sa mga qubit: nag-iimbak ito ng mga ladder operator sa mga mode, at ang isang bosonic mode ay kayang humawak ng napakaraming particle. Lahat ng nagpapahangganan sa operator (kung ilang occupation level ang itatago mo, at kung paano ilalatag ang mga level na iyon sa mga qubit) ay napagpapasyahan kapag ima-map mo ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The library mapper [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") works in the occupation (Fock) basis: level $n$ of a mode is the state with $n$ bosons. It takes the operator and a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"), which holds the truncation and the encoding. This guide explains what those two choices mean and what each one costs. For an end-to-end route that uses them, see [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started); for how the transpiler applies the same choices to a whole circuit, see [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Ang library mapper na [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") ay gumagana sa occupation (Fock) basis: ang level $n$ ng isang mode ay ang estado na may $n$ boson. Kinukuha nito ang operator at isang [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"), na may hawak ng truncation at ng encoding. Ipinapaliwanag ng gabay na ito kung ano ang ibig sabihin ng dalawang pagpiling iyon at kung ano ang gastos ng bawat isa. Para sa buong daloy na gumagamit ng mga ito, tingnan ang [Mag-simulate ng Bose-Hubbard dynamics na may pagpili ng encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started); para malaman kung paano inilalapat ng transpiler ang parehong mga pagpili sa buong circuit, tingnan ang [Mag-transpile ng mga bosonic circuit](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"truncation-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Truncate the Fock space {#truncate-the-fock-space}"
msgstr "I-truncate ang Fock space {#truncate-the-fock-space}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mode that is kept to $d = n_\\text{max} + 1$ levels, where $n_\\text{max}$ is its `max_occupation`, no longer obeys the canonical commutation relation. Writing $\\bar{b}$ for the annihilation operator truncated to those levels,\n"
msgstr "Ang isang mode na itinatago sa $d = n_\\text{max} + 1$ na mga level, kung saan ang $n_\\text{max}$ ay ang `max_occupation` nito, ay hindi na sumusunod sa canonical commutation relation. Kung isusulat natin ang $\\bar{b}$ para sa annihilation operator na na-truncate sa mga level na iyon,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[\\bar{b}, \\bar{b}^\\dagger] = 1 - d \\, \\lvert d-1 \\rangle\\langle d-1 \\rvert \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[\\bar{b}, \\bar{b}^\\dagger] = 1 - d \\, \\lvert d-1 \\rangle\\langle d-1 \\rvert \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so the relation holds on every level except the highest <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id4). You can see this by mapping the commutator of the two ladder operators and reading its diagonal on the levels of one mode. The following helper builds the dense matrix of a mapped operator for a single mode, which is only reasonable for very small registers:\n"
msgstr "kaya totoo ang relasyon sa bawat level maliban sa pinakamataas <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id4). Makikita mo ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-map sa commutator ng dalawang ladder operator at pagbasa sa diagonal nito sa mga level ng isang mode. Binubuo ng sumusunod na helper ang dense matrix ng isang na-map na operator para sa isang mode, na makatwiran lang para sa napakaliliit na register:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last entry is $1 - d$. Because this means the span of $\\{\\bar{b}^\\dagger, \\bar{b}\\}$ is not closed under the commutator, no encoding is an isomorphism of algebras. An encoding maps *states*, together with the operators that act within the truncated subspace. The following two consequences matter in practice.\n"
msgstr "Ang huling entry ay $1 - d$. Dahil ang ibig sabihin nito ay hindi sarado sa ilalim ng commutator ang span ng $\\{\\bar{b}^\\dagger, \\bar{b}\\}$, walang encoding na isomorphism ng mga algebra. Ang encoding ay nagma-map ng mga *estado*, kasama ang mga operator na kumikilos sa loob ng na-truncate na subspace. Mahalaga sa praktika ang sumusunod na dalawang konsekwensya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The cutoff must bound the reachable occupation.** It is not enough to bound the occupation you start with. A beamsplitter acting on $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ populates $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ and $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, so a cutoff of one silently produces a wrong state:\n"
msgstr "**Dapat sakop ng cutoff ang occupation na maaabot.** Hindi sapat na sakop lang nito ang occupation na sinimulan mo. Ang beamsplitter na kumikilos sa $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ ay nagpupuno sa $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ at $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, kaya ang cutoff na isa ay tahimik na gagawa ng maling estado:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With a cutoff of one, the probability of staying in $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ is one, because the two states that the dynamics would populate do not exist. With a cutoff of two, it vanishes, which is the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect. This is why `max_occupation` is a required argument that never has a default: it is a modeling decision and a convergence parameter that you are expected to sweep.\n"
msgstr "Sa cutoff na isa, ang probability na manatili sa $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ ay isa, dahil hindi umiiral ang dalawang estado na pupunuin sana ng dynamics. Sa cutoff na dalawa, nawawala ito, na siyang Hong-Ou-Mandel effect. Kaya ang `max_occupation` ay required na argument na walang default: isa itong desisyon sa modeling at isang convergence parameter na inaasahang i-sweep mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mapping does not commute with normal ordering.** The operators $b b^\\dagger$ and $b^\\dagger b + 1$ are equal before truncation, but they map to different qubit operators:\n"
msgstr "**Hindi nagko-commute ang mapping sa normal ordering.** Magkapantay ang mga operator na $b b^\\dagger$ at $b^\\dagger b + 1$ bago ang truncation, pero iba ang qubit operator na kinalalabasan nila kapag na-map:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two agree on every level but the highest. Applied to the top level, $b^\\dagger$ has nowhere to go and the amplitude is clipped, so $b b^\\dagger$ is zero there, whereas $b^\\dagger b + 1$ gives $d$. Decide once whether your Hamiltonian is defined in normal-ordered form, and map that form consistently.\n"
msgstr "Magkapareho ang dalawa sa bawat level maliban sa pinakamataas. Kapag inilapat sa pinakamataas na level, walang mapupuntahan ang $b^\\dagger$ at napuputol ang amplitude, kaya zero ang $b b^\\dagger$ doon, samantalang $d$ ang ibinibigay ng $b^\\dagger b + 1$. Magdesisyon nang minsan kung naka-define sa normal-ordered na anyo ang Hamiltonian mo, at i-map ang anyong iyon nang pare-pareho.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three methods help you choose a cutoff, and all of them are lower bounds. The operator reports the largest number of creation operators that it applies to each mode within a single term, and a spec compares that with its cutoffs:\n"
msgstr "Tatlong paraan ang tumutulong sa iyong pumili ng cutoff, at lahat ng mga ito ay lower bound. Iniuulat ng operator ang pinakamalaking bilang ng mga creation operator na inilalapat nito sa bawat mode sa loob ng isang term, at ikinukumpara ito ng isang spec sa mga cutoff nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A non-zero entry means the cutoff is below the bound, and the value is how far. These helpers do not know about the dynamics, so a passing check does not make a cutoff sufficient; the beamsplitter above has a bound of one yet needs a cutoff of two. They can also report a shortfall for a term that is zero on the retained levels, as $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger b b$ is for a cutoff of one.\n"
msgstr "Ang non-zero na entry ay nangangahulugang mas mababa ang cutoff sa bound, at ang value ay kung gaano kalayo. Walang alam ang mga helper na ito sa dynamics, kaya hindi nagiging sapat ang cutoff dahil lang pumasa ang check; ang beamsplitter sa itaas ay may bound na isa pero nangangailangan ng cutoff na dalawa. Puwede rin silang mag-ulat ng kakulangan para sa isang term na zero sa mga natirang level, gaya ng $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger b b$ para sa cutoff na isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"level-spec-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec {#describe-the-truncation-with-a-levelspec}"
msgstr "Ilarawan ang truncation gamit ang LevelSpec {#describe-the-truncation-with-a-levelspec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") bundles the cutoff of every mode with the encoding, and it derives from them how many qubits each mode occupies and where its qubits start. Everything that has to agree about that (the mapper, the transpiler layout, the state preparation) is given the same spec. The encoding is a required argument, and so is the cutoff: neither has a default.\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama ng isang [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") ang cutoff ng bawat mode at ang encoding, at hinuhugot nito mula sa mga iyon kung ilang qubit ang sinasakop ng bawat mode at kung saan nagsisimula ang mga qubit nito. Ang lahat ng kailangang magkasundo tungkol doon (ang mapper, ang layout ng transpiler, ang state preparation) ay binibigyan ng iisang spec. Required ang encoding, at ganoon din ang cutoff: walang default ang alinman sa dalawa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cutoff is either one integer, shared by all modes, or one integer per mode:\n"
msgstr "Ang cutoff ay alinman sa isang integer na ibinabahagi ng lahat ng mode, o isang integer para sa bawat mode:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spec built from a single integer leaves the number of modes open, so you have to resolve it before asking for widths. A sequence is never broadcast, whatever its length, and it fixes the number of modes:\n"
msgstr "Ang spec na binuo mula sa iisang integer ay nag-iiwan na bukas ang bilang ng mga mode, kaya kailangan mo itong i-resolve bago humingi ng mga lapad. Hindi kailanman ibino-broadcast ang isang sequence, anuman ang haba nito, at itinatakda nito ang bilang ng mga mode:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mode $m$ occupies the qubits `offsets[m]` to `offsets[m] + widths[m] - 1`, so modes with different cutoffs can take different numbers of qubits, and the offsets are the running sum of the widths. You do not need to pass the number of modes to the mapper. It takes it from the spec, or, for a spec with a single cutoff, from the operator through [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\"). The register can be wider than the modes need; the surplus qubits are idle and sit at the end:\n"
msgstr "Sinasakop ng mode $m$ ang mga qubit mula `offsets[m]` hanggang `offsets[m] + widths[m] - 1`, kaya ang mga mode na magkakaiba ang cutoff ay puwedeng kumuha ng magkakaibang bilang ng mga qubit, at ang mga offset ay ang running sum ng mga lapad. Hindi mo kailangang ipasa sa mapper ang bilang ng mga mode. Kinukuha nito iyon mula sa spec, o, para sa spec na may iisang cutoff, mula sa operator sa pamamagitan ng [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\"). Puwedeng mas malapad ang register kaysa sa kailangan ng mga mode; ang sobrang mga qubit ay idle at nasa dulo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator that acts on a mode beyond the last one of a per-mode spec is refused:\n"
msgstr "Tinatanggihan ang operator na kumikilos sa mode na lampas sa huli ng isang per-mode na spec:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A few limits follow from how the encodings count qubits. Under a compact encoding, a mode with a single level (`max_occupation = 0`) takes no qubit at all, because its one level needs nothing to be told apart from another. Such a mode is allowed and does not move the qubits of the modes after it, but a spec in which every mode would take no qubit is rejected. The unary encodings hold at most 128 levels per mode, and a larger cutoff raises an error that suggests a compact encoding:\n"
msgstr "May ilang limitasyon na nagmumula sa kung paano nagbibilang ng mga qubit ang mga encoding. Sa ilalim ng compact encoding, ang mode na may iisang level (`max_occupation = 0`) ay hindi kumukuha ng kahit isang qubit, dahil walang kailangan ang nag-iisang level nito para maibukod sa iba. Pinapayagan ang ganoong mode at hindi nito ginagalaw ang mga qubit ng mga mode na kasunod nito, pero tinatanggihan ang spec kung saan walang qubit na kukunin ang bawat mode. Ang mga unary encoding ay may hawak na hanggang 128 level kada mode lang, at ang mas malaking cutoff ay nagtataas ng error na nagmumungkahi ng compact encoding:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose an encoding {#choose-an-encoding}"
msgstr "Pumili ng encoding {#choose-an-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") decides which basis state of a block of qubits represents each level. There are four, and no one of them is best in general <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). The number of qubits per mode and the bit pattern of each level follow from the encoding:\n"
msgstr "Tinutukoy ng isang [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") kung aling basis state ng isang bloke ng mga qubit ang kumakatawan sa bawat level. Apat ang mayroon, at wala sa mga ito ang pinakamahusay sa pangkalahatan <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). Ang bilang ng mga qubit kada mode at ang bit pattern ng bawat level ay sumusunod sa encoding:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bit patterns are integers in which bit $q$ is the value of qubit $q$. The unary encodings spend one qubit per level and set one of them. The compact encodings spend $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ qubits and store the level number, in binary or as a Gray code in which neighboring levels differ in one bit. The string name of an encoding is accepted wherever the encoding is.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga bit pattern ay mga integer kung saan ang bit $q$ ay ang value ng qubit $q$. Ang mga unary encoding ay gumagastos ng isang qubit kada level at isa lang ang itinatakda. Ang mga compact encoding ay gumagastos ng $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ na mga qubit at iniimbak ang numero ng level, sa binary o bilang Gray code kung saan ang magkatabing level ay nagkakaiba sa isang bit. Tinatanggap ang string name ng isang encoding kahit saan tinatanggap ang encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trade-off is qubits against operator weight. The compact encodings need exponentially fewer qubits, but a ladder operator connects levels whose patterns can differ in several bits, so its terms act on more qubits. The following sections look at what this costs, starting with the two unary encodings, which have identical layouts and differ only in the operator.\n"
msgstr "Ang trade-off ay mga qubit laban sa bigat ng operator. Mas kaunting qubit nang exponential ang kailangan ng mga compact encoding, pero ang ladder operator ay nag-uugnay ng mga level na ang mga pattern ay puwedeng magkaiba sa ilang bit, kaya mas maraming qubit ang kinikilusan ng mga term nito. Tinitingnan ng mga sumusunod na seksyon kung magkano ang gastos nito, simula sa dalawang unary encoding, na magkapareho ang layout at ang operator lang ang pagkakaiba.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"unary-variants-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the two unary encodings {#compare-the-two-unary-encodings}"
msgstr "Ihambing ang dalawang unary encoding {#compare-the-two-unary-encodings}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the unary encoding a ladder operator moves one excitation between two neighboring qubits. To write that as an operator on the whole mode, you must choose what to do with the other qubits. The two variants choose differently:\n"
msgstr "Sa unary encoding, inililipat ng ladder operator ang isang excitation sa pagitan ng dalawang magkatabing qubit. Para maisulat iyon bilang operator sa buong mode, kailangan mong piliin kung ano ang gagawin sa iba pang mga qubit. Magkaiba ang pinipili ng dalawang variant:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`unary_projected` puts a projector $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ on every other qubit of the mode. That enforces the one-hot constraint in the operator itself: the term acts only if the rest of the mode is empty.\n"
msgstr "Naglalagay ang `unary_projected` ng projector na $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ sa bawat iba pang qubit ng mode. Ipinapatupad nito ang one-hot constraint sa mismong operator: kumikilos lang ang term kung walang laman ang natitirang bahagi ng mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`unary_unprojected` leaves those qubits alone, so the term acts as the identity on them.\n"
msgstr "Hindi ginagalaw ng `unary_unprojected` ang mga qubit na iyon, kaya identity ang kilos ng term sa mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look at a single $b^\\dagger$ at $d = 4$ under both. The mapper returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), whose terms are strings of single-qubit bit terms. Here are the first four terms of each, with the qubits they act on:\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang isang $b^\\dagger$ sa $d = 4$ sa ilalim ng dalawa. Nagbabalik ang mapper ng isang [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), na ang mga term ay mga string ng single-qubit na bit term. Narito ang unang apat na term ng bawat isa, kasama ang mga qubit na kinikilusan ng mga ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both have twelve terms with the same coefficients. The projected terms carry a `0` bit term on the two qubits that the unprojected terms do not mention, so each projected term touches all four qubits and each unprojected term touches two. In general a projected term touches all $d$ qubits of the mode, because it carries two factors, each $X$ or $Y$, and a projector on each other qubit.\n"
msgstr "Parehong may labindalawang term na may parehong mga coefficient ang dalawa. Ang mga projected na term ay may `0` na bit term sa dalawang qubit na hindi binabanggit ng mga unprojected na term, kaya ang bawat projected na term ay humahawak sa lahat ng apat na qubit at ang bawat unprojected na term ay sa dalawa. Sa pangkalahatan, ang projected na term ay humahawak sa lahat ng $d$ na qubit ng mode, dahil may dala itong dalawang factor, bawat isa ay $X$ o $Y$, at isang projector sa bawat iba pang qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two operators are equal on the states that the encoding is meant for, the one-hot basis states (the codewords), and differ outside them. To check, take a small operator on two modes at $d = 3$ and compare the matrices on the nine codewords:\n"
msgstr "Magkapantay ang dalawang operator sa mga estadong nilalayon ng encoding, ang mga one-hot basis state (ang mga codeword), at nagkakaiba sa labas ng mga ito. Para masuri, kumuha ng maliit na operator sa dalawang mode sa $d = 3$ at ikumpara ang mga matrix sa siyam na codeword:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both also leave the codeword subspace invariant, so a state prepared on a codeword stays on codewords. The choice matters only for states that leave that subspace, for example through noise. There the projected operator suppresses the evolution, because its projectors fail, whereas the unprojected one keeps acting. Neither behavior is a physical requirement. The unprojected operator is only defined on the one-hot subspace, so choosing it is a modeling decision and not a free optimization.\n"
msgstr "Parehong pinananatiling invariant ng dalawa ang codeword subspace, kaya ang estadong inihanda sa isang codeword ay nananatili sa mga codeword. Mahalaga lang ang pagpili para sa mga estadong lumalabas sa subspace na iyon, halimbawa dahil sa ingay. Doon, pinipigilan ng projected na operator ang evolution, dahil pumapalya ang mga projector nito, samantalang patuloy na kumikilos ang unprojected. Hindi pisikal na pangangailangan ang alinman sa dalawang gawi. Ang unprojected na operator ay naka-define lang sa one-hot subspace, kaya ang pagpili nito ay desisyon sa modeling at hindi libreng optimization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the projectors cost is gates. Evolve a Hermitian $b^\\dagger + b$ on one mode for a short time, and count the two-qubit gates after Qiskit’s transpilation:\n"
msgstr "Ang gastos ng mga projector ay mga gate. I-evolve ang isang Hermitian na $b^\\dagger + b$ sa isang mode sa maikling panahon, at bilangin ang mga two-qubit gate pagkatapos ng transpilation ng Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The exact counts depend on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gate, which changes between releases, so plot them:\n"
msgstr "Nakadepende ang eksaktong bilang sa kung paano sini-synthesize ng Qiskit ang evolution gate, na nagbabago sa bawat release, kaya i-plot ang mga ito:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![CX count against the number of levels d for the four encodings. The unary\\_projected count grows fastest, the unary\\_unprojected count grows linearly, and the Gray code is the cheapest.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/mappers-14.avif)\n"
msgstr "![CX count against the number of levels d for the four encodings. The unary\\_projected count grows fastest, the unary\\_unprojected count grows linearly, and the Gray code is the cheapest.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/mappers-14.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unprojected count grows linearly with $d$, because each of the $d - 1$ transitions is a two-qubit rotation. The projected count grows much faster, because every term acts on all $d$ qubits. The compact encodings need fewer qubits, but the weight of their terms depends on how the bit patterns of neighboring levels differ: the Gray code, in which they differ in one bit, is the cheaper of the two compact encodings, and standard binary jumps when a carry flips several bits at once ($d = 5$). Whether a compact encoding also beats the unprojected unary one depends on $d$ and on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution, so read the trend and not the ranking at one size.\n"
msgstr "Linear na lumalaki ang bilang ng unprojected kasabay ng $d$, dahil ang bawat isa sa $d - 1$ na transition ay isang two-qubit rotation. Mas mabilis na lumalaki ang bilang ng projected, dahil bawat term ay kumikilos sa lahat ng $d$ na qubit. Mas kaunting qubit ang kailangan ng mga compact encoding, pero ang bigat ng mga term nila ay nakadepende sa kung paano nagkakaiba ang mga bit pattern ng magkatabing level: ang Gray code, kung saan nagkakaiba sila sa isang bit, ang mas mura sa dalawang compact encoding, at tumatalon ang standard binary kapag maraming bit ang sabay na binabaligtad ng isang carry ($d = 5$). Kung natatalo rin ng compact encoding ang unprojected na unary ay nakadepende sa $d$ at sa kung paano sini-synthesize ng Qiskit ang evolution, kaya basahin ang trend at hindi ang ranggo sa isang laki.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The projectors also matter when you expand a mapped operator into Paulis, which [`from_sparse_observable()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_observable) does by replacing each projector with a sum of two Pauli operators. A term with $k$ projectors becomes $2^k$ Pauli terms. Here is a single $b^\\dagger$ at small $d$, which is the only size at which you should try this:\n"
msgstr "Mahalaga rin ang mga projector kapag pinalalawak mo ang na-map na operator sa mga Pauli, na ginagawa ng [`from_sparse_observable()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_observable) sa pamamagitan ng pagpapalit sa bawat projector ng kabuuan ng dalawang Pauli operator. Ang term na may $k$ na projector ay nagiging $2^k$ na Pauli term. Narito ang isang $b^\\dagger$ sa maliit na $d$, na siya lang laki kung saan dapat mong subukan ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both variants store the same number of terms, but the expansion of the projected one grows exponentially in $d$. For anything larger than a toy example, read the terms of the [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) directly, as the listing above does, instead of converting it.\n"
msgstr "Pareho ang bilang ng mga term na iniimbak ng dalawang variant, pero exponential sa $d$ ang paglaki ng expansion ng projected. Para sa anumang mas malaki sa isang toy example, basahin nang direkta ang mga term ng [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), gaya ng ginawa ng listahan sa itaas, sa halip na i-convert ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The compact encodings cannot drop their projectors. There the zero bits are part of the level number, so removing a $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ changes which levels a term connects, and the operator is no longer the same on the codewords. This is why only the unary encoding comes in two variants.\n"
msgstr "Hindi maaaring alisin ng mga compact encoding ang mga projector nila. Doon, bahagi ng numero ng level ang mga zero bit, kaya ang pag-alis ng $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ ay nagbabago sa kung aling mga level ang iniuugnay ng term, at hindi na pareho ang operator sa mga codeword. Kaya unary encoding lang ang may dalawang variant.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A product of ladders is truncated first {#a-product-of-ladders-is-truncated-first}"
msgstr "Ang produkto ng mga ladder ay tinutruncate muna {#a-product-of-ladders-is-truncated-first}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One more design choice shows up in the cost of diagonal terms. The mapper does not map each ladder operator and multiply the results. It collects the ladder operators that a term applies to one mode, multiplies them as a $d \\times d$ matrix in the Fock basis, truncates that product once, and encodes the result <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). A product such as the number operator $b^\\dagger b$ therefore stays diagonal:\n"
msgstr "May isa pang pagpili sa disenyo na lumalabas sa gastos ng mga diagonal na term. Hindi ima-map ng mapper ang bawat ladder operator at imumultiply ang mga resulta. Kinokolekta nito ang mga ladder operator na inilalapat ng isang term sa isang mode, imumultiply ang mga ito bilang $d \\times d$ na matrix sa Fock basis, tinutruncate ang produktong iyon nang isang beses, at ine-encode ang resulta <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). Kaya ang produkto tulad ng number operator na $b^\\dagger b$ ay nananatiling diagonal:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its terms are the projectors $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 1 \\rvert$ on the qubit of each level above zero, weighted by the level number (level zero has weight zero and so has no term). A time evolution of it is a set of single-qubit rotations and needs no two-qubit gate. Multiplying the two mapped ladder operators instead gives the same operator on the codewords, but a different one outside them, with off-diagonal strings that cost gates:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga term nito ay ang mga projector na $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 1 \\rvert$ sa qubit ng bawat level na mas mataas sa zero, na tinitimbang ng numero ng level (ang level zero ay may bigat na zero kaya walang term). Ang time evolution nito ay isang set ng mga single-qubit rotation at hindi nangangailangan ng two-qubit gate. Ang pagmu-multiply sa dalawang na-map na ladder operator ay nagbibigay ng parehong operator sa mga codeword, pero ibang operator sa labas ng mga ito, na may mga off-diagonal na string na may gastos na mga gate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonal terms such as the on-site interaction of the Bose-Hubbard model are these products, which is where this choice matters.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga diagonal na term tulad ng on-site interaction ng Bose-Hubbard model ay ang mga produktong ito, kaya dito mahalaga ang pagpiling ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a custom mapper {#write-a-custom-mapper}"
msgstr "Sumulat ng custom na mapper {#write-a-custom-mapper}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want an encoding that the library does not provide, build it from the image of a single ladder operator. [`map_boson_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-map-boson-action-generators#qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators\") takes a function that maps one [`BosonAction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-action-boson-action#qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction \"qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction\"), a function that returns the identity, and builds the mapper of whole operators from them. It multiplies the images of the actions of each term in order, scales by the coefficient, and sums the terms. The output can be any type that supports scalar multiplication and composition.\n"
msgstr "Kung gusto mo ng encoding na hindi ibinibigay ng library, buuin ito mula sa image ng isang ladder operator. Ang [`map_boson_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-map-boson-action-generators#qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators\") ay kumukuha ng function na nagma-map ng isang [`BosonAction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-action-boson-action#qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction \"qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction\"), isang function na nagbabalik ng identity, at binubuo mula sa mga ito ang mapper ng buong mga operator. Imumultiply nito ang mga image ng mga action ng bawat term ayon sa pagkakasunod-sunod, ini-scale sa coefficient, at isinusuma ang mga term. Ang output ay puwedeng anumang uri na sumusuporta sa scalar multiplication at composition.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As an example, take the encoding for $d = 2$ that stores a mode in one qubit. A creation operator is $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$, which is $(X - iY)/2$ in Qiskit’s convention, and an annihilation operator is its adjoint:\n"
msgstr "Bilang halimbawa, kunin ang encoding para sa $d = 2$ na nag-iimbak ng isang mode sa isang qubit. Ang creation operator ay $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$, na $(X - iY)/2$ sa convention ng Qiskit, at ang annihilation operator ay ang adjoint nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This hand-written mapper multiplies the mapped ladder operators, and it agrees with the library mapper here because every mode has two levels and a qubit holds the whole mode. At larger $d$, as the previous section showed, composing the mapped ladders and truncating the product first are not the same operator outside the codewords.\n"
msgstr "Ang hand-written na mapper na ito ay nagmu-multiply ng mga na-map na ladder operator, at sumasang-ayon ito sa library mapper dito dahil may dalawang level ang bawat mode at hawak ng isang qubit ang buong mode. Sa mas malaking $d$, gaya ng ipinakita ng nakaraang seksyon, hindi magkapareho ang operator sa labas ng mga codeword kapag kinomposo muna ang mga na-map na ladder at kapag tinruncate muna ang produkto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use such a mapper in a circuit, wrap it in a function with the signature `(operator, num_qubits) -> SparseObservable` and hand it to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), which maps the operator of every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate with it. The transpiler pipeline is described in [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Para gamitin ang ganoong mapper sa isang circuit, balutin ito sa isang function na may signature na `(operator, num_qubits) -> SparseObservable` at ibigay ito sa [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), na nagma-map gamit ito sa operator ng bawat [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate. Inilalarawan ang transpiler pipeline sa [Mag-transpile ng mga bosonic circuit](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two details are worth knowing. First, the qubit operator must have real coefficients, because [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) rejects an imaginary part. A Hermitian operator maps to a real one, but only once the terms that cancel have been merged. This hand-written mapper does not merge them, so a hopping term and its adjoint leave imaginary coefficients behind until you simplify the result. The library mapper merges its own result; a custom one has to do it, for example by wrapping it in [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\"):\n"
msgstr "Dalawang detalye ang dapat malaman. Una, dapat may totoong mga coefficient ang qubit operator, dahil tinatanggihan ng [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) ang imaginary na bahagi. Ang Hermitian na operator ay nagma-map sa totoo, pero kapag nai-merge na lang ang mga term na nagka-cancel. Hindi ito minemerge ng hand-written na mapper na ito, kaya ang hopping term at ang adjoint nito ay nag-iiwan ng mga imaginary na coefficient hangga't hindi mo pinapasimple ang resulta. Minemerge ng library mapper ang sarili nitong resulta; ang custom ay kailangang gawin ito, halimbawa sa pamamagitan ng pagbabalot dito gamit ang [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second, a product formula synthesizes the terms in the order it receives them, and the order a mapper produces is not guaranteed to be stable. The helpers [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\") and [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") wrap a mapper function to control it: `simplify` merges duplicate strings and sorts the terms into a canonical order, whereas `group_wise` maps one group of the operator at a time so that the terms of a group stay adjacent. Do not combine the two, because sorting discards the grouping. The [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) shows how to assign groups, and the [synthesis guide](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows how the order affects the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ikalawa, sini-synthesize ng product formula ang mga term ayon sa pagkakasunod-sunod ng pagtanggap nito, at hindi garantisadong stable ang pagkakasunod-sunod na ginagawa ng mapper. Ang mga helper na [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\") at [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") ay bumabalot sa mapper function para kontrolin ito: ang `simplify` ay nagme-merge ng mga duplicate na string at inaayos ang mga term sa canonical na pagkakasunod-sunod, samantalang ang `group_wise` ay nagma-map ng isang group ng operator nang paisa-isa para manatiling magkakatabi ang mga term ng isang group. Huwag pagsamahin ang dalawa, dahil sinisira ng sorting ang grouping. Ipinapakita ng [gabay sa grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation) kung paano magtalaga ng mga group, at ipinapakita ng [gabay sa synthesis](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) kung paano naaapektuhan ng pagkakasunod-sunod ang circuit.\n"

